WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.888 --> 00:00:23.521
Before you start: disposable MSP SLA policy for White Rabbit (SLA settings)

2
00:00:23.521 --> 00:00:29.488
1. Configure and persist the customer-to-MSP priority mapping

3
00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:40.867
2. Escalation starts the MSP obligation (not initial visibility)

4
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:54.364
3. Change the mapping: existing targets stay, new escalation uses current config

5
00:00:54.364 --> 00:01:06.102
4. MSP returns ticket 1 to the customer; history preserved

6
00:01:06.102 --> 00:01:18.595
5. Departed relationship: Kansas Farms keeps its own outcome; MSP live read unavailable

7
00:01:18.595 --> 00:01:19.990
5. Breach/routing notification (in-app and SMTP sink)
